Linux Fundamentals — Hack The Box
Astructured collection of notes, commands, and concepts I learned while completing the Linux Fundamentals track on Hack The Box. This repository demonstrates my understanding of Linux internals, command‑line navigation, permissions, processes, and basic system administration — all essential skills for cybersecurity and penetration testing.
Overview

The Linux Fundamentals modules strengthened my ability to:

  Navigate and interact with Linux systems using the command line

  Understand the Linux filesystem hierarchy

  Manage users, groups, and permissions

  Work with processes and services

  Use essential tools for cybersecurity workflows

  Apply Bash commands to analyze, manipulate, and control system behavior
Linux Filesystem: 
/etc — configuration files

/var — logs and variable data

/home — user directories

/bin, /sbin, /usr/bin — essential binaries
Key commands:
pwd
ls -la
cd /path
cat
find / -name filename

File Permissions:
chmod 755 script.sh
chown user:group file.txt
umask 022
useradd, userdel
passwd
sudo -l
groups
id
Networking:
ip a
ip r
ping
netstat -tulnp
curl / wget

